EXERCISE 2
he following function finds the missing number from an array of integers;
that is, the array is expected to have all integers from 0 up to the array’s
length, but one is missing. As examples, the array [5, 2, 4, 1, 0] is missing
the number 3, and the array [9, 3, 2, 5, 6, 7, 1, 0, 4] is missing the number 8.
Here’s an implementation that is O(N2) (the clause if number not in array is
itself already O(N), since the computer needs to search the entire array
to find number):

def find_missing_number(array):
for number in range(len(array) + 1):
if number not in array:
return number
return None

Use sorting to write a new implementation of this function that only takes
O(N log N). (Some other implementations are even faster, but we’re
focusing on using sorting as a technique to make code faster.)

answer:
ok let me understand this
so we have a function that finds missing number from array of ints
array is expected to have all integers from 0 up to n (array length)

example input = [5,2,4,1,0] -> number 3 is missing
example input = [9,3,2,5,6,7,1,0,4] -> number 8 is missing
so it only cares about 1 missing number?

and we have the python implmenetation which is quadratic n^2
let me try to analyze those, im shit at python

seems like it has 2 loops here? outer is a range thing
and the inner check is also a loop which cross checks that
range with all of the inputs

question wants me to do  n log n, lets try this in racket

|#

; listof number -> number
; lets assume xs is nonempty
; functional style/list style
(define (find-missing-number xs)
  ; just compare each element to its index,
  ; since the list of number starts from 0
  (let ((sorted-xs (sort xs <)))
    (define (helper lst i)
      (cond [(null? lst) i]
            [(equal? i (car lst))
             (helper (cdr lst) (+ i 1)) ]; continue
            [else i]
            )
      )

    ; initialize helper with index 0
    (helper sorted-xs 0)
    
    )
  )
(display 'find-missing-number)(newline)
(find-missing-number '(5 2 4 1 0)) ; should return 3
(find-missing-number '(9 3 2 5 6 7 1 0 4)) ; should return 8

; vector -> number
; vector/imperative style
(define (find-missing-number-v2 vect)
  (let ((n (- (vector-length vect) 1))
        (sorted-vect (vector-sort vect <)))
    
    (define (helper i v)
      (cond [(> i n) i] ;for guard/theres no missing number
            [else (let ((x (vector-ref v i)))
                    (if (equal? x i)
                        (helper (+ i 1) v)
                        i
                        )
                    )]
            )
      )
    (helper 0 sorted-vect)
    
    )
  )
(find-missing-number-v2 (vector 5 2 4 1 0))
(find-missing-number-v2 (vector 9 3 2 5 6 7 1 0 4))



